Control flow chooses or repeats actions. if runs code when a condition is true; for repeats over items; while repeats while a condition holds. A function is a named block that takes inputs, called arguments, and returns an output. Functions avoid repetition and make code testable. Example in Python:
def mean(values):
    return sum(values) / len(values)
print(mean([2, 4, 6]))
The output is 4.0.
